{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Come on in, Mr. Hale. What brings you in?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Check-up.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): You're sixty-two, yeah?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll think out loud, if you don't mind. The main thing on your chart is high blood pressure.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): Still taking the pressure pill? That's the lisinopril.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): The nurse read your med list this morning as twenty milligrams of the pressure pill, lisinopril, once a day. Is that the dose?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Ten.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ten milligrams? Her note says twenty. You're sticking with ten?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Ten.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): Um, two numbers and no bottle, so I won't guess the dose. You do take it every day?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): High blood pressure for about five-ish years, on this pill the whole time?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): And the aspirin?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Sometimes.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Baby aspirin, eighty-one milligrams. It was every day for your heart, but you take it on and off?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any medicine allergies?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any chest pain?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Short of breath at all?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): What about climbing stairs, or walking fast?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Tight.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): A tight feeling in the chest?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): With the stairs and with walking fast, both?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Both.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): Settles if you stop and rest?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): When did that start?",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): Dunno.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): Um, could it be months?",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): Maybe.",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (DOCTOR): So that's a tight feeling in the chest with stairs or fast walking, better with rest, for months maybe, and you can't date the start. Right?",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any sweating, nausea, or pain down the arm with it?",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0045] person_1 (DOCTOR): Heartburn or other stomach stuff?",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0047] person_1 (DOCTOR): Your dad had heart disease, didn't he?",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0049] person_1 (DOCTOR): Let me check you. Pressure is one thirty-six over eighty-four, pulse seventy-two. Heart regular, no murmur, lungs clear. You comfortable right now?",
  "[SEG0050] person_2 (PATIENT): Fine.",
  "[SEG0051] person_1 (DOCTOR): I was gonna just see you next year and skip the workup, or maybe order a chest x-ray. Well, actually, lungs are clear, so scratch the x-ray. I also nearly added a troponin, but you're fine sitting here, so not that either. What I do want today, for this exertional tightness, is an ECG, plus bloods, a basic metabolic panel and a lipid panel.",
  "[SEG0052] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0053] person_1 (DOCTOR): If the tightness comes on at rest, or you get sweaty or sick with it, go to the ER. Bring the pressure-pill bottle next time, and I'll see you in two weeks. My working thought is this exertional chest tightness could be angina, but that is not a firm diagnosis."
 ],
